{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_ga7ftn7obqnrlzacoxvrjgplg2xwi5nbdwfvx562vw4kkuoexsea","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01AJnSyFyqfJSwBHT4iW8dsT","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-m8wKRn/translated_rust/ERRORS.md","content":"# ERRORS.md — error-surface table (Phase A.2)\n\n## Mechanical derivation\n\nEvery non-comment line of C source, in full (there is no other C code):\n\n```c\n/* c_src/src/sillymain.h */               /* c_src/src/sillymain.c */\n#ifndef SILLYMAIN_H_                      #include <stdio.h>\n#define SILLYMAIN_H_                      #include \"sillymain.h\"\nint helloworld();                         int helloworld() {\n#endif //SILLYMAIN_H_                         printf(\"Hello World!\\n\");\n                                              return 0;\n/* c_src/src/main.c */                    }\n#include \"sillymain.h\"\nint main() {\n    return helloworld();\n}\n```\n\nGrep for every rejection construct the task lists:\n\n| construct grepped | hits in `c_src/` |\n|---|---|\n| `RETURN_ERROR` / error macros / error enums | 0 |\n| `return -1` / negative or sentinel returns | 0 (`return 0;` and `return helloworld();` only) |\n| `return NULL` | 0 |\n| `assert` | 0 |\n| explicit range / bounds check (`if`, `switch`, `?:`, `goto`) | 0 — the sources contain **no** conditional or branch of any kind |\n| null-pointer check | 0 (no function takes a pointer; no pointer variable exists) |\n| min/max constant, magic limit | 0 |\n| `errno` inspection | 0 |\n| `#ifdef` / `#if` build switch | 0 apart from the `SILLYMAIN_H_` include guard |\n| function parameters that could be invalid | 0 — both functions take no parameters |\n\nSo **the C library rejects nothing and cannot fail**: there is no input to\nvalidate. That is a finding, not an excuse to skip Phase C — the rows below are\nthe failure modes the C code *does* have (they come from the discarded `printf`\nresult and from what an FFI caller can legally throw across the boundary at an\nunprototyped, parameterless C function), plus the generic boundaries required by\nthe task. Every row is a real, executable differential test.\n\n## Error-surface table\n\n| # | function | trigger (the exact invalid input/condition) | expected C result | test | [x] |\n|---|----------|---------------------------------------------|-------------------|------|-----|\n| 1 | `helloworld` | `printf` fails with `ENOSPC`: fd 1 redirected to `/dev/full`. The return value of `printf` is discarded by `sillymain.c`. | returns `0`; no abort, no `errno` propagation | `err01_helloworld_enospc_dev_full` | [x] |\n| 2 | `helloworld` | `printf` fails with `EBADF`: fd 1 **closed** before the call, so the underlying `write(2)` has no file description. | returns `0` | `err02_helloworld_ebadf_closed_fd1` | [x] |\n| 3 | `helloworld` | `printf` fails with `EBADF`: fd 1 redirected to a fd opened **`O_RDONLY`** (open file description not writable). | returns `0` | `err03_helloworld_ebadf_readonly_fd1` | [x] |\n| 4 | `helloworld` | `printf` fails with `EPIPE`: fd 1 is the write end of a pipe whose read end is closed (`SIGPIPE` explicitly set to `SIG_IGN` for both callees, so the failure surfaces as an error rather than a signal). | returns `0`; process survives | `err04_helloworld_epipe_broken_pipe` | [x] |\n| 5 | `helloworld` | Repeated call *after* a failed call (row 1–4 left the stream's error indicator set: glibc keeps `stdout` in error state, so the retry also fails). | still returns `0`, every time | `err05_helloworld_repeat_after_failure` | [x] |\n| 6 | `main` | Same as rows 1–4 but through `main`, whose value **is** `helloworld()`'s value — a non-zero propagation would be an exit-status divergence. | returns `0` | `err06_main_write_failures_propagate_zero` | [x] |\n| 7 | `helloworld` | Extra arguments passed across the FFI boundary. `int helloworld();` is an *unprototyped* (K&R) declarator, so a C caller may legally call it with any arguments; they must be ignored. Called through `extern \"C\" fn(c_int, *const c_void, f64, u64, ...) -> c_int` signatures. | returns `0`, arguments ignored, no stack corruption | `err07_extra_args_ignored` | [x] |\n| 8 | `main` | Extra arguments across the FFI boundary, incl. the conventional `int main(int, char**)` shape called with `argc = -1` / `argv = NULL` (an out-of-range `argc` and a null pointer — the C `main()` declares no parameters and must ignore both). | returns `0` | `err08_main_extra_args_and_null_argv` | [x] |\n| 9 | `helloworld` | Null / garbage pointer arguments pushed across the boundary (`0x1`, `usize::MAX`, `NULL`) — the closest analogue of \"null pointer\" for an API that takes no pointers: they must never be dereferenced. | returns `0`, no segfault | `err09_null_and_garbage_pointer_args` | [x] |\n| 10 | `helloworld` | Out-of-range \"enum\" value across the FFI boundary. The C API declares no enum, so the generic case is exercised: an `int` argument with no valid variant (`i32::MIN`, `-1`, `0x7fff_ffff`, `0xdead_beef` reinterpreted) passed to the unprototyped function. | returns `0`, value ignored | `err10_out_of_range_enum_values` | [x] |\n| 11 | `helloworld` / `main` | Zero-length and oversized \"length\" arguments (`0`, `usize::MAX`, `isize::MIN`) across the boundary — the generic length boundary for an API with no length parameter. | returns `0`, ignored | `err11_zero_and_oversized_lengths` | [x] |\n| 12 | `helloworld` | Return value inspected as the full 64-bit register instead of `int`. The C function returns `int`, so only the low 32 bits are defined; both libraries must agree on the `c_int` value. | low 32 bits are `0` for both (the high half is ABI-undefined and is *not* compared — documented, not asserted) | `err12_return_value_is_c_int_zero` | [x] |\n| 13 | `helloworld` | Called re-entrantly / concurrently from several threads while the stream is in error state. C stdio lock